  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ITP 308 SGU Mine Water and Mine Waste Management - Mine Water and Mine Waste 2017, 18,19,20,21 AVSLUTAD</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ITP 308 SGU Tillsyn av avfall och vattenf&#xf6;roreningar fr&#xe5;n gruvor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsens avsedda effekt &#xe4;r att h&#xf6;ja kapacitet och kunskap hos nyckelpersoner inom institutioner organisationer med mandat att reglera och p&#xe5;verka utsl&#xe4;pp till vatten fr&#xe5;n gruvdrift och mineralutvinningens f&#xf6;roreningar till vatten. I f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngningen antas att dessa nyckelpersoner kan p&#xe5;verka den institutionella kontexten och f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningarna f&#xf6;r en milj&#xf6;m&#xe4;ssigt, demokratiskt och socialt god styrning av gruvindustri och mineralutvinning.

By the end of 2025, the program is expected to have contributed to six outcomes related to the participating partner organisations:
1. Efficient and ethical governance principles within partner organisations leading to a sustainable mining sector with increased accountability. 
2. Effective dissemination and knowledge transfer of sustainable mineral extraction and its contribution to local and national development. 
3. Partner organisations ensure the best possible scrutiny of environmental impacts, prevention and mitigation at all stages of the mine cycle.
4. Partner organisations use transparent, inclusive, and meaningful dialogue to ensure full public participation. 
5. Gender discrepancy is continuously targeted within the partner organisations.
6. Strengthened collaboration between partner organisations within and between the participating countries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sveriges Geologiska Unders&#xf6;kning (SGU) har tillsammans med Naturv&#xe5;rdsverket och Lule&#xe5; tekniska universitet (LTU) inkommit med ett f&#xf6;rslag till ett internationellt kapacitetsutvecklingsprogram (ITP) inriktad p&#xe5; att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten hos kontrollmyndigheter som utf&#xf6;r tillsyn av gruvor med speciellt fokus p&#xe5; avfall och det vatten som sprider f&#xf6;roreningar fr&#xe5;n avfallet. Kapacitetsutvecklingsrogrammet &#xe4;r &#xe4;ven &#xf6;ppet f&#xf6;r &#xf6;vriga relevanta deltagare ur civila samh&#xe4;llet, privata sektorn och akademin.

Insatsens f&#xf6;reslagna budget i programf&#xf6;rslaget &#xe4;r SEK 59 072 348 och ska genomf&#xf6;ras under &#xe5;ren 2017- 2024. De planerade programomg&#xe5;ngarna om 25 deltagare (maximalt 30) vardera &#xe4;r i dagsl&#xe4;get. Sida tar beslut om SEK 60 100 000 f&#xf6;r att &#xe4;ven m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra planerings-och rekryteringsfas i samband med inkludering av nya l&#xe4;nder. Avtalet styr vilken motprestation avtalsparten beh&#xf6;ver g&#xf6;ra f&#xf6;r att nyttja denna post. Inom ramen f&#xf6;r befintlig budget kan &#xe4;ven SGU i dialog med Sida genomf&#xf6;ra riktade kortkurser, exempelvis f&#xf6;r deltagande organisationers/institutioners chefer eller s&#xe4;rskilda training of trainers-satsningar.

Initialt fokuserar programmet p&#xe5; tre l&#xe4;nder som har en viktig och v&#xe4;xande mineralutvinning - Etiopien, Tanzania och Zambia. F&#xf6;rstudien innefattade &#xe4;ven en baslinje-bed&#xf6;mning av Rwanda, Mocambique, Mano-regionen (Elfenbenskusten, Guinea, Liberia och Sierra Leone). Programmet riktar sig till tj&#xe4;nstem&#xe4;n p&#xe5; relevanta myndigheter i ovan n&#xe4;mnda l&#xe4;nder, samt relevanta akt&#xf6;rer ur civila samh&#xe4;llet, privata sektorn samt akademien.

Programmet avser att st&#xf6;dja ber&#xf6;rda tillsynsmyndigheter i arbetet med att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra sin leverans av tj&#xe4;nster genom interna f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsprocesser. Genom att inkludera relevanta akt&#xf6;rer fr&#xe5;n civila samh&#xe4;llet, privata sektorn och akademien; i s&#xe5;v&#xe4;l deltagandet som genom f&#xf6;rel&#xe4;sningar, studiebes&#xf6;k etc, skapas en &#xf6;kad m&#xf6;jlighet att adressera komplexiteten i sektorn och vikten av att binda in en bred akt&#xf6;rsgrupp.

Programmet &#xe4;r uppbyggt s&#xe5; att det dels ger en introduktion av &#xf6;vergripande principer f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rvaltning, milj&#xf6;m&#xe5;l, milj&#xf6;lagstiftning, anti-korruption, &#xf6;ppen data och naturresursf&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning; samt erbjuder den vetenskapliga och tekniska bakgrund som kr&#xe4;vs f&#xf6;r att deltagarna ska kunna ta fram underlag f&#xf6;r bed&#xf6;mningar. En viktig f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttning f&#xf6;r en god f&#xf6;rvaltning och h&#xe5;llbar ekonomisk utveckling &#xe4;r kompetenta och kunniga offentliga organisationer/institutioner som agerar med integritet och som kan uppr&#xe4;tth&#xe5;lla r&#xe4;ttss&#xe4;kerhet. Deltagarna f&#xe5;r under programmets g&#xe5;ng v&#xe4;gledning i genomf&#xf6;randet av egna f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsprojekt f&#xf6;rankrade i respektive hemorganisation/institution. Genom utbyten mellan deltagare fr&#xe5;n olika l&#xe4;nder kan deltagarna ocks&#xe5; st&#xe4;rka sina n&#xe4;tverk och utbyta kunskaper och l&#xe4;rdomar.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Swedish Geological Survey (SGU) has together with the Swedish Environmental Protection Agency and Lule&#xe5; University of Technology (LTU) submitted a proposal for an international capacity development program (ITP) aimed at strengthening the capacity of control authorities that carry out inspections of mines with special focus on waste and the water that spreads. contaminants from the waste. The capacity development program is also open to other relevant participants from civil society, the private sector and academia.
The initiative&apos;s proposed budget in the program proposal is SEK 59,072,348 and will be implemented during the years 2017-2024. The planned program rounds of 25 participants (maximum 30) each are at present. Sida decides on SEK 60,100,000 to also enable the planning and recruitment phase in connection with the inclusion of new countries. The agreement governs what consideration the contractor needs to make to use this item. Within the framework of the existing budget, SGU can also, in dialogue with Sida, conduct targeted short courses, for example for the heads of participating organizations / institutions or special training of trainers initiatives.

Initially, the program focuses on three countries that have important and growing mineral extraction - Ethiopia, Tanzania and Zambia. The feasibility study also included a baseline assessment of Rwanda, Mozambique, the Mano region (C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire, Guinea, Liberia and Sierra Leone). The program is aimed at officials of relevant authorities in the above-mentioned countries, as well as relevant actors from civil society, the private sector and academia.

The program intends to support relevant regulatory authorities in the work of improving their service delivery through internal change processes. By including relevant actors from civil society, the private sector and academia; in both participation and through lectures, study visits, etc., an increased opportunity is created to address the complexity of the sector and the importance of binding a broad group of actors.

The program is structured so that it provides an introduction to overall principles for management, environmental goals, environmental legislation, anti-corruption, open data and natural resource supply; and offers the scientific and technical background required for the participants to be able to produce a basis for assessments. An important prerequisite for good governance and sustainable economic development is competent and knowledgeable public organizations / institutions that act with integrity and that can maintain legal certainty. During the program, the participants receive guidance in the implementation of their own change projects anchored in each home organization / institution. Through exchanges between participants from different countries, participants can also strengthen their networks and exchange knowledge and lessons learned.</narrative>
  </description>
